## 3. Meta Ads Architecture & Template Structure

### A. Campaign Hierarchy (Account Level)
1. **[TOF-ASC] Advantage+ Shopping / Prospecting Campaign (CBO)**
   - Objective: Sales / Conversions (Purchase optimization).
   - Budget: 60-70% of total Meta budget.
   - Targeting: Broad (Country / Age / Gender only, algorithmic audience discovery).
   - Existing Customer Budget Cap: Set to 5%–10% max to preserve prospecting purity.
2. **[TEST-SANDBOX] Creative Testing Engine (ABO)**
   - Objective: Conversions (Purchase or Lead).
   - Budget: 20% of Meta budget.
   - Structure: Dynamic Creative Testing (DCT) ad sets — 3 videos/images, 2 primary texts, 2 headlines per ad set.
   - Graduation Criteria: Winning creative with CPA ≤ \$35 and ≥ 35 purchases graduates into the TOF-ASC campaign.
3. **[MOF/BOF] Warm Engagement & Cart Abandonment**
   - Audiences: 30-day IG/FB engagers, 50%+ video viewers, 14-day Add-to-Cart non-buyers.
   - Creative Angle: User-generated content (UGC), founder stories, risk-reversal guarantees, customer review carousels.
4. **[RET-DPA] Catalog Sales (Dynamic Product Ads)**
   - Audiences: Viewed content or Added to Cart in last 14 days (excluding 30-day purchasers).

### B. Ad Creative Structure (The 3-Second Hook Rule)
- **Format Mix**: 60% 9:16 vertical video (Reels/Stories), 30% 1:1 or 4:5 feed creatives, 10% multi-card carousel.
- **Hook (0-3s)**: Stop-the-scroll visual pattern interrupt + on-screen caption hook.
- **Hold (3-15s)**: Problem agitation, mechanism of action, before/after contrast.
- **Offer (15-30s)**: Irresistible proposition, bundle discount, social proof, friction-free CTA.

